course: dictionary
lesson: 5865
title: Who is the manager?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A manager is a person who is in charge. To work out what a manager does, look at the words around the word. «Picture a stage manager in a split costume five minutes before curtain-up saying, "Bit of a pickle."» A stage manager is in charge of the show behind the stage, so manager means a person who runs something.
explain: A manager can be in charge of a shop, a business, a team of workers, or a project. In football, the manager is the person in charge of the whole team. Ask yourself: what is this person in charge of? The clues in the sentence will tell you.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you read «Picture a stage boss in a split costume», the sentence still makes sense, so you are on the right track. When you know the meaning, the word becomes easy to use.
fact: A manager is a person who is in charge of something.
fact: Managers can run a shop, a business, a team of workers, a project or a sports team.
fact: «Manager» is a noun: one manager, many managers.
fact: «Stage manager» is a job that runs the show backstage in a theatre.
fact: Many jobs today, like «social media manager», did not exist 30 years ago.
exercise: «Picture a stage manager in a split costume five minutes before curtain-up.» What is a stage manager in charge of? | A bank full of money | A bus full of passengers | *The show on stage | A garden of flowers
exercise: «Many jobs today, like social media manager, did not exist 30 years ago.» In football, what does the team manager do? | Sells the tickets at the gate | Cuts the grass on the pitch | Blows the whistle to start the game | *Chooses the team
exercise: «For example, "We are streamlining the team" from a manager usually means some people are about to lose their jobs.» What does this message usually suggest? | The team is going on holiday | Everyone is getting a pay rise | The team has a new kit | *Some people may lose their jobs
test: Which phrase means the person in charge of a shop? | Shop customer | *Shop manager | Shop assistant | Shop window
test: Which phrase means the person in charge of a sports team? | Team kit | Team bus | *Team manager | Team player
exam: Which word is the plural of manager? | *managers | manageres | managerss | managerren
